From: frapercan <frapercan1@alum.us.es>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:51:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Restrict delete_queues and queue monitoring to the task's
 own queues

delete_queues called delete_all_queues(), which removes every queue on the
broker through the HTTP API, including those of other tasks, applications
and users, along with their pending messages. Two FANTASIA users sharing a
RabbitMQ server wiped each other's work.

Add delete_task_queues(), which deletes only this task's computing and
inserting queues and its per-model computing queues (<computing_queue>_*)
in the connection's vhost, and use it for delete_queues.
delete_all_queues() is kept unchanged for callers that rely on it.

monitor_queues() used a substring match, so a task whose queue name
contained another task's name waited on that task's queues. It now uses the
same filter.

Verified against RabbitMQ: a foreign queue with a pending message survives a
FANTASIA run with delete_queues: true, while the task's own queues are
reset.
